On your Bastion node, create a new folder structure called my-nginx-chart:
mkdir -p my-nginx-chart/templates

2. Create Chart.yaml
This file satisfies the metadata requirement that Helm was looking for earlier. Create it at the root of your chart directory:
my-nginx-chart/Chart.yaml
apiVersion: v2 
name: my-nginx-chart 
description: A reusable Nginx web deployment 
type: application 
version: 0.1.0 
appVersion: "1.25"

3. Create values.yaml
This file isolates the variables (like replica counts and image tags) so you can change them easily without modifying the core code.
my-nginx-chart/values.yaml
replicaCount: 1 
image: 
repository: nginx 
tag: latest 
pullPolicy: Always 
service: 
type: NodePort 
port: 80 
targetPort: 80

4. Create the Parameterized Templates
Now, we will split your original manifest into two clean templates inside the templates/ directory, replacing the hardcoded text fields with Helm variables ({{ ... }}).
my-nginx-chart/templates/deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: {{ .Release.Name }}-nginx
  namespace: {{ .Release.Namespace }}
spec:
  replicas: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: {{ .Release.Name }}-nginx
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: {{ .Release.Name }}-nginx
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: "{{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.image.tag }}"
        imagePullPolicy: {{ .Values.image.pullPolicy }}
        ports:
        - containerPort: {{ .Values.service.targetPort }}

The Service Template:
my-nginx-chart/templates/service.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: {{ .Release.Name }}-service
  namespace: {{ .Release.Namespace }}
spec:
  type: {{ .Values.service.type }}
  selector:
    app: {{ .Release.Name }}-nginx
  ports:
  - name: http
    port: {{ .Values.service.port }}
    targetPort: {{ .Values.service.targetPort }}


5. Deploy with Helm!
Now that your project matches a legitimate Helm blueprint layout, you can verify it and install it smoothly from your Bastion node.
First, use tree to make sure your workspace matches this look:
tree my-nginx-chart
